From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LibreScoot <librescoot@example.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Mar 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fbcon: show boot logo regardless of console loglevel

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [embedded platform workaround]

The fbcon code suppresses the boot logo when console_loglevel is at or
below CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET (4).  This forces embedded systems to use
loglevel >= 5 to see the logo, which also prints warning messages over
the logo on the display.

Remove the loglevel check so the boot logo displays even with 'quiet'
or low loglevel, allowing a clean full-screen logo with no text.

Signed-off-by: LibreScoot <librescoot@example.com>
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/core/fbcon.c
@@ -1004,9 +1004,6 @@
 	info = fbcon_info_from_console(vc->vc_num);
 
-	if (logo_shown < 0 && console_loglevel <= CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL_QUIET)
-		logo_shown = FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW;
-
 	if (vc != svc || logo_shown == FBCON_LOGO_DONTSHOW ||
 	    (info->fix.type == FB_TYPE_TEXT))
 		logo = 0;
 
